KG42.register("rules-26e6c98f36355afc23a5cccd",{"id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R010","paper":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R010","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Market payment","process_stage":"settlement","market_meaning":"The coordinator provides and operates the billing mechanisms associated with the trading platform. Scope: P2P energy-sharing framework within an energy sharing region. Trades are settled using the status at the last iteration, retaining P2P energy sharing on that basis. Scope: The paper's last-defence mechanism for iterative P2P energy sharing. Condition: The maximum number of iterations is reached without convergence. Trading is settled at the deadline at which the bidding and pricing iteration has to stop. Scope: Practical settlement deadline discussed in support of the last-defence mechanism. Condition: The deadline for the bidding and pricing iteration is reached.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function settlement.payment under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["coordination.local_operator","settlement.payment"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R010-E001","source":"coordination.local_operator","target":"settlement.payment","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R010-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"settlement","context_text":"P2P energy-sharing framework within an energy sharing region. | Practical settlement deadline discussed in support of the last-defence mechanism. | The paper's last-defence mechanism for iterative P2P energy sharing.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g02-e19","v141-b-g03-E15"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R010-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The coordinator provides and operates the billing mechanisms associated with the trading platform. Scope: P2P energy-sharing framework within an energy sharing region.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g02-e04"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R010-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Trades are settled using the status at the last iteration, retaining P2P energy sharing on that basis. Scope: The paper's last-defence mechanism for iterative P2P energy sharing. Condition: The maximum number of iterations is reached without convergence.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e19","v141-b-g03-E15","v141-b-g04-EV09"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R010-C003","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Trading is settled at the deadline at which the bidding and pricing iteration has to stop. Scope: Practical settlement deadline discussed in support of the last-defence mechanism. Condition: The deadline for the bidding and pricing iteration is reached.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E15","v141-b-g02-e19"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e05","location":{"location_id":"src-d485825b0d-p04-c2r3__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":4,"printed_page":"996","section":"3.1","anchor_text":"gy sharing paradigm d P2P energy sharing paradigms. P2P energy sharing can be carried out among pros","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"P2P energy sharing can be carried out among prosumers in a microgrid or a part of distribution network (referred to as \"energy sharing region (ESR)\" in this paper), supervised by a market operator (named \"energy sharing coordinator\", short as \"coordinator\", in this paper). A coordinator is usually needed in P2P energy sharing practice due to two reasons. First of all, a coordinator is needed to specify the rules for trading and supervise the energy sharing activities. The rules include the core pricing model and implementation process, as well as other relevant rules to guarantee the interests of every participant. Secondly, a trading platform as well as the associated metering and billing mechanisms needs to be provided and operated by a coordinator, based on which P2P energy sharing is able to be conducted."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e19","location":{"location_id":"src-d485825b0d-p07-c2r2__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.3","anchor_text":"gy y g p g d- market mechanisms they designed [13,15,17,37]. C) If convergence cannot always be guar","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"exception"},"source_text":"If convergence cannot always be guaranteed, an exit mechanism is usually designed in P2P energy sharing mechanisms, as that in Ref. [17], because in real life participants need to settle their trades ﬁnally and cannot just wait forever, although the speciﬁcs of the exit mechanism can vary. For example, in Ref. [17], if the simulation does not converge when the maximum number of iterations is reached, then the simulation is forced to exit, and all the prosumers are considered to directly trade with the retailer individually instead (i.e. P2P energy sharing is not used given divergence). For the exit mechanism used in this paper (which will be detailed later in Section 3.3.4), the simulation is also forced to exit at the maximum number of iterations if not converge, but the status at the last iteration is used for settling trades (i.e. P2P energy sharing is still used based on the results of the last iteration)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E15","location":{"location_id":"src-d485825b0d-p10-c1r2__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":10,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.3.4","anchor_text":"p p p p they achieve that, but not to ﬁgure out how they can achieve that. ca th 3.3.4. Last-defence","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-10.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"The proposed last-defence mechanism is just to end the simulation after a pre-defined finite number of iterations, no matter the convergence is achieved or not. If the simulation ends in that way, the status at the last iteration is used in this paper to calculate the index values for evaluation. It is fair to do so because in practice, the bidding and pricing iteration cannot carry on forever and there is a deadline at which the iteration has to stop and the trading is settled. … In the proposed last-defence mechanism, the maximum number of iterations allowed is an important parameter, and should be chosen to be large enough so that the simulation is not forced to be stopped before it converges. However, there is no way to decide a perfect maximum number of iterations a priori … Therefore, heuristic values are used in this paper."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e04","location":{"location_id":"src-d485825b0d-p04-c2r3__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.1","anchor_text":"gy sharing paradigm d P2P energy sharing paradigms. P2P energy sharing can be carried out among pros","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"P2P energy sharing can be carried out among prosumers in a microgrid or a part of distribution network (referred to as “energy sharing region (ESR)” in this paper), supervised by a market operator (named “energy sharing coordinator”, short as “coordinator”, in this paper). A coordinator is usually needed in P2P energy sharing practice due to two reasons. First of all, a coordinator is needed to specify the rules for trading and supervise the energy sharing activities. The rules include the core pricing model and implementation process, as well as other relevant rules to guarantee the interests of every participant. Secondly, a trading platform as well as the associated metering and billing mechanisms needs to be provided and operated by a coordinator, based on which P2P energy sharing is able to be conducted."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g04-EV09","location":{"location_id":"src-d485825b0d-p14-c1r2__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":14,"printed_page":null,"section":"5.2.1","anchor_text":"pp pp y p customer owned an appliance was a result of the sampling from a given probability distribu","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-14.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"The maximum number of iterations was set as 200 as a part of the last-defence mechanism as discussed in Section 3.3.4."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":"No design-selection or operational decision variable is defined for this market-payment/settlement rule in the frozen graph or supplied evidence. The source states institutional obligations and conditional settlement procedures, so x is empty without asserting that the source lacks variables elsewhere.","empty_theta_reason":"No fixed numeric or symbolic parameter is defined for this payment rule in the supplied evidence. The maximum iteration count is discussed as a heuristic last-defence/coordination parameter and a case-study value, not as a source-symbol-defined parameter of settlement.payment; therefore theta is empty."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-coordination"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"settlement.payment","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e05","quote":"a trading platform as well as the associated metering and billing mechanisms needs to be provided and operated by a coordinator"}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e19","quote":"the simulation is also forced to exit at the maximum number of iterations if not converge, but the status at the last iteration is used for settling trades (i.e. P2P energy sharing is still used based on the results of the last iteration)."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E15","quote":"in practice, the bidding and pricing iteration cannot carry on forever and there is a deadline at which the iteration has to stop and the trading is settled."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"20f1a788077d27b418d9f8c72acdb5a5cd593eac8a6aac4ab62a258268996767","applicability":"non_mathematical","reason":"The supplied evidence for v141-c-R010 contains only procedural settlement/payment statements: the coordinator provides and operates billing mechanisms, last-defence settlement uses the status at the last iteration, and trading is settled at the practical deadline. No mathematical expression, decision variable, fixed parameter, optimization role, or source symbol is defined for this payment rule in the frozen graph or supplied evidence. Existing phi entries therefore remain not_formalized with null expressions. This assessment relies on unreviewed B candidate evidence and does not claim independent source verification.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R010-C001","node_ids":["coordination.local_operator","settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R010-E001"],"rationale":"Frozen edge E001 links coordination.local_operator to settlement.payment; the evidence states that the coordinator provides and operates the associated billing mechanisms, which is a procedural settlement/payment obligation rather than a mathematical expression."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R010-C002","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R010-E001"],"rationale":"The last-defence fallback affects the settlement.payment node under the coordinator-to-payment relationship represented by E001; the evidence supports a conditional settlement choice by last-iteration status without supplying variables or a formal equation."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R010-C003","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R010-E001"],"rationale":"The practical deadline condition concerns the settlement.payment node and its coordination context via E001; the source states a procedural deadline for stopping the bidding/pricing iteration and settling trades, not a mathematical constraint."}],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
